1. Main Menu

Description:

The main menu serves as the entry point of the Banking Management System, allowing users to navigate to customer management, account management, transaction management, reports, and exit options through a simple console-based interface.

2. Customer Management

Description:

The Customer Management module enables users to add, view, search, update, and delete customer records. It ensures efficient management of customer information with input validation and exception handling.

3. Account Management

Description:

The Account Management module allows users to create new bank accounts, view account details, check balances, and manage account information while maintaining data consistency in the database.

4. Transaction Management

Description:

The Transaction Management module supports essential banking operations such as deposits, withdrawals, and fund transfers. Every transaction is securely recorded in the database and can be retrieved for future reference.

5. Reports

Description:

The Reports module provides an overview of banking operations by displaying statistics such as total customers, total accounts, highest and lowest balances, total deposits, total withdrawals, and transaction reports in a well-formatted tabular view.
